do","pattern":"gerundio (circulando, conduciendo)","explain":"*circulando* = while driving along. It sets the situation in which the rule applies.","markers":["circulando","conduciendo","adelantando"],"hits":586,"pct":9.2,"sentenceIds":[]},{"id":"gsiempreque","title":"Condición: siempre que / cuando","pattern":"cuando / siempre que","explain":"*siempre que* means *provided that*, not *always*. It is a condition and it takes the subjunctive.","markers":["siempre que","cuando"],"hits":416,"pct":6.5,"sentenceIds":["sb0c93def64","s81e2b3354d","s7b1a57cbc5","s6f93e86166","sa0d6a94bb3","s34581e10b7","s66ed77d1db","s465d3477e7","sa39176fa04","s65ec3d7b02","s243f6ba932","s6654c28a78","s4fe1cb2644","sc4a950968e","sdeff0a9433","s50c78550f9","sa051a50e8b","sb20ae23af0","s0d28c5509f","s88285f9395","s0c803df6e0","sacda2aae43","s93cb39fc48","sc6eacfafb6"]},{"id":"gsi","title":"Condicional con «si»","pattern":"condicional: si ...","explain":"*si* + present tense decides which rule applies. The condition is the whole question.","markers":["si"],"hits":316,"pct":5.0,"sentenceIds":["s86ba892782","sd192f578bd","sb0c93def64","s6756b7b8fe","s06862ee0b2","s833b1817b5","sa6343ceae4","se985ac2f3a","s7b1a57cbc5","s8f96921ac6","s8b5f6864a3","s2c3e886d13","s9b65c5d7b1","s72e9b623f3","s416f3ec8d8","sc0607c5c49","s2b1141b07f","s73daa620aa","sbad0e918e5","se0f49b57e5","se9f620038c","s2242083522","sa355136508","saa2392894e","s85c3056be8","scbb9ba436c","s6e913fa2cf","se42c1c7211","s66ed77d1db","s465d3477e7","s532adbd5d1","s6d40c99ed8","s8ef0beaaeb","s639492f7ca","s7a7b3921a2","s81c5bc27c5","s81924c6597","s477c02f54c","s6eeacc4d79","scb7afdbad7"]},{"id":"gse","title":"El «se» impersonal","pattern":"pasiva refleja (se + verbo)","explain":"*se debe*, *se permite*, *se prohíbe* = one must, it is allowed, it is forbidden. No named subject — the rule applies to everybody.","markers":["se debe","se permite","se prohíbe","se considera"],"hits":308,"pct":4.8,"sentenceIds":["sd192f578bd","s6756b7b8fe","s06862ee0b2","s81e2b3354d","s7b1a57cbc5","s9b65c5d7b1","s7989c2570d","s332b15735b","seae4c3ceb4","s66ed77d1db","s465d3477e7","s243f6ba932","s9a7a9728dc","s239f237c03","s21fc4c8704","s702290d166","sf8dae14860","s5749c4c4a8","sd46f43c52f","s3d585fa301","s299104211e","s28a73df898","s437bb96c46","s2653d1cb1e","s89c55cf19c","sea14881bf6","sd5b1c67bb7","s986989d3e5","s67e67284be"]},{"id":"gpermiso","title":"Permitido · prohibido · obligatorio","pattern":"está permitido / prohibido","explain":"The three words the exam builds its traps on. They appear 138 / 111 / 103 times in your corpus.","markers":["está permitido","está prohibido","obligatorio"],"hits":266,"pct":4.2,"sentenceIds":["sd192f578bd","sb0c93def64","s833b1817b5","sa6343ceae4","s8b5f6864a3","s2c3e886d13","s2242083522","saa2392894e","s9bec75fecb","sb9f1280913","sf14857ae40","s232b581449","s5da786f376","s88285f9395","sf40f85c754","s128da5b43f"]},{"id":"gnormagen","title":"Como norma general","pattern":"'como norma general'","explain":"This phrase warns you in advance that exceptions exist. Look for the exception before you answer.","markers":["como norma general"],"hits":62,"pct":1.0,"sentenceIds":[]},{"id":"gsalvo","title":"Excepciones: salvo / excepto","pattern":"excepción: salvo / excepto / a menos que","explain":"*salvo* and *excepto* introduce the case where the rule does NOT apply. Miss the word and you invert the answer. It is the single most common way a DGT question flips.","markers":["salvo","excepto","a menos que","salvo que"],"hits":57,"pct":0.9,"sentenceIds":["sf120496a72","sa6343ceae4","s73daa620aa","s9bec75fecb","sb601344eed","sf8dae14860","sdbc2bf702e","s10861782eb","see3d4f4201","s1811eac8a8","s78e1d727d7","sf66d49b60f","s1a1581194b","s0b1b6c5b61","s3230a645ae","s7880fe63db","s182fa56537","s038109a8bd","sf40f85c754","s128da5b43f","s37c55d4847"]},{"id":"glimites","title":"Al menos vs como máximo","pattern":"superlativo/límite: al menos, como mínimo, como máximo","explain":"*al menos* / *como mínimo* set a floor; *como máximo* sets a ceiling. Reading one as the other reverses the answer.","markers":["al menos","como mínimo","como máximo"],"hits":45,"pct":0.7,"sentenceIds":["sdda73123d6"]},{"id":"gningun","title":"Negación absoluta","pattern":"negación doble: no ... ni / en ningún caso","explain":"*en ningún caso* = under no circumstances. Absolute wording is often, but not always, the wrong option.","markers":["en ningún caso","nunca","ni"],"hits":42,"pct":0.7,"sentenceIds":["s86ba892782","sb0c93def64","s06862ee0b2","s833b1817b5","sa6343ceae4","s81e2b3354d","s41edc1bfcb","s72e9b623f3","sf7b5044048","se0ff52e3e0","s332b15735b","s3143431b03","se9f620038c","sa355136508","s85c3056be8","seae4c3ceb4","s66ed77d1db","sdda73123d6","sa39176fa04","s532adbd5d1","s4c31a9ca6d","s8ef0beaaeb","s16304be12d","s65ec3d7b02","s243f6ba932","s7a7b3921a2","s477c02f54c","s6eeacc4d79","sb801b3d22a","sf8dae14860","s4eda49fc6e","s6654c28a78","s4fe1cb2644","s1f43e821a8","s5749c4c4a8","s8a21cb412e","s10d5de8a63","s1d6a3ade3e","s2f9fdf3352","s6c013f1114"]},{"id":"gaunque","title":"Concesión: aunque","pattern":"concesiva: aunque","explain":"*aunque* = although / even if. What follows does not cancel the rule: «debes adaptar la velocidad aunque circules por debajo del límite».","markers":["aunque","aun cuando"],"hits":29,"pct":0.5,"sentenceIds":["s2242083522","s86b3102f79","sa41e92aafa","sfd91f17f0a","sfccd3dc553"]}]